
<p>Describe what you've built in Go at a production level: what did the service do and how long were you working in Go?</p>(optional)
While working in Tesla, I worked on a production platform thats written completely in Go Lang and it was serving around 80,000 monthly users. I completely owned the Dgraph integration as an extension for our platform to server as a V2 layer for the applications need deep relations. I worked from technical evolution, vendor engagement to migration of existing applications. 

<p>Walk me through a time you iterated on a feature based on direct customer feedback: what changed and why?</p>(optional)
In Tesla, we had setup sometime every month to visit one customer (another internal teams) and evaluate there business and how they are leveraging the use of our platforms and increase there capacity. When we went to the delivery center to asses we realized one of the main blockers they have is on approval flow changes, when they submit an approval change or want to add a new incentive for customers, they have to wait for our developer team to make the changes and deploy and that delays the process. On emergencies they manually do it and updates the system later. we addressed this by building a separate evaluation engine that managers can access directly and from there they can add / auto approve the changes which removes the dependency on our team.  
